1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,127
Part 1 Man: Hello. Do you mind if I ask you some questions about your journey today?

2
00:00:06,127 --> 00:00:08,290
We're doing a customer satisfaction survey.

3
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:12,700
Sophie: Yes. OK. I've got about ten minutes before my train home leaves

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,190
I'm on a day trip.

5
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:18,730
Man: Great. Thank you. So first of all, could you tell me your name?

6
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:20,710
Sophie: It's Sophie Bird.

7
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:24,460
Man: Thank you. And would you mind telling me what you do?

8
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:25,910
Sophie: I'm a journalist.

9
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:28,200
Man: Oh really? That must be interesting.

10
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,560
Sophie: Yes. It is.

11
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:33,370
Man: So was the reason for your visit here today work?

12
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:37,330
Sophie: Actually, it's my day off. I came here to do some shopping.

13
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:38,400
Man: Oh right.

14
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,070
Sophie: But I do sometimes come here for work.

15
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:46,350
Man: OK. Now I'd like to ask some questions about your journey today, if that's OK.

16
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:47,580
Sophie: Yes. No problem.

17
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:52,000
Man: Right, so can you tell me which station you're travelling back to?

18
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,360
Sophie: Staunfirth, where I live.

19
00:00:54,360 --> 00:01:04,050
Man: Can I just check the spelling? S-T-A-U-N-F-I-R-T-H?

20
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:04,790
Sophie: That's right.

21
00:01:04,790 --> 00:01:08,420
Man: And you travelled from there this morning?

22
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:09,320
Sophie: Yes.

23
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:13,485
Man: OK, good. Next, can I ask what kind of ticket you bought?

24
00:01:13,485 --> 00:01:17,650
I assume it wasn't a season ticket, as you don't travel every day.

25
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:21,701
Sophie: That's right. No, I just got a normal return ticket.

26
00:01:21,701 --> 00:01:26,120
I don't have a rail card so I didn't get any discount.

27
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:29,080
I keep meaning to get one because it's a lot cheaper.

28
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:32,580
Man: Yes - you'd have saved 20% on your ticket today

29
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:35,820
So you paid the full price for your ticket?

30
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:38,270
Sophie: I paid £23.70.

31
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:41,190
Man: OK. Do you think that's good value for money?

32
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:45,710
Sophie: Not really. I think it's too much for a journey that only takes 45 minutes.

33
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:48,300
Man: Yes, that's one of the main complaints we get

34
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:51,420
So, you didn't buy your ticket in advance?

35
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:54,880
Sophie: No. I know it's cheaper if you buy a week in advance

36
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:56,710
but I didn't know I was coming then.

37
00:01:56,710 --> 00:02:02,350
Man: I know. You can't always plan ahead. So, did you buy it this morning?

38
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:04,500
Sophie: No, it was yesterday.

39
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,690
Man: Right. And do you usually buy your tickets at the station?

40
00:02:08,690 --> 00:02:12,480
Sophie: Well, I do usually but the ticket office closes early

41
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:14,890
and I hate using ticket machines.

42
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:17,764
I think ticket offices should be open for longer hours.

43
00:02:17,764 --> 00:02:21,500
There's always a queue for the machines and they're often out of order.

44
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,330
Man: A lot of customers are saying the same thing.

45
00:02:24,330 --> 00:02:29,250
Sophie: So to answer your question... I got an e-ticket online.

46
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:35,206
Man: OK. Thank you. Now I'd like to ask you about your satisfaction with your journey.

47
00:02:35,206 --> 00:02:39,300
So what would you say you were most satisfied with today?

48
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:42,216
Sophie: Well, I like the wifi on the train.

49
00:02:42,216 --> 00:02:47,400
It's improved a lot. It makes it easier for me to work if I want to.

50
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:50,040
Man: That's the first time today anyone's mentioned that

51
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,550
It's good to get some positive feedback on that.

52
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:53,340
Sophie: Mmm.

53
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:57,430
Man: And, is there anything you weren't satisfied with?

54
00:02:57,430 --> 00:03:01,960
Sophie: Well, normally, the trains run on time and are pretty reliable

55
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:04,810
but today there was a delay;

56
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:08,090
the train was about 15 minutes behind schedule.

57
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:10,240
Man: OK. I'll put that down

58
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:15,010
Now I'd also like to ask about the facilities at this station.

59
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:18,420
You've probably noticed that the whole station's been upgraded

60
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,620
What are you most satisfied with?

61
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:30,130
Sophie: I think the best thing is that they've improved the amount of information about train times etc. that's given to passengers.

62
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:33,574
- it's much clearer - before there was only one board

63
00:03:33,574 --> 00:03:37,400
and I couldn't always see it properly - which was frustrating.

64
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:41,440
Man: That's good. And is there anything you're not satisfied with?

65
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:46,012
Sophie: Let's see... I think things have generally improved a lot.

66
00:03:46,012 --> 00:03:51,000
The trains are much more modern and I like the new café.

67
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:56,640
But one thing is that there aren't enough places to sit down, especially on the platforms.

68
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:59,960
Man: OK - so I'll put 'seating' down

69
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:02,230
shall I, as the thing you're least satisfied with?

70
00:04:02,230 --> 00:04:03,870
Sophie: Yes. OK.

71
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:09,048
Man: Can I ask your opinion about some of the other facilities?

72
00:04:09,048 --> 00:04:11,280
We'd like feedback on whether people are satisfied

73
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:15,090
dissatisfied or neither satisfied nor dissatisfied.

74
00:04:15,090 --> 00:04:16,260
Sophie: OK.

75
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:19,500
Man: What about the parking at the station?

76
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:24,160
Sophie: Well to be honest, I don't really have an opinion as I never use it.

77
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:27,860
Man: So, neither satisfied nor dissatisfied for that then.

78
00:04:27,860 --> 00:04:30,210
Sophie: Yes, I suppose so...

79
00:04:30,210 --> 00:04:31,000
Man: OK, and what about...?
